  "question": {
    "text": "A neutron collides elastically with the stationary nucleus of an atom of mass number <math><mi>A</mi></math>.&nbsp;If the collision is perfectly elastic, then after the collision the fraction of the initial kinetic energy retained by the neutron, is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let us assume the mass of the neutron is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;and mass of the nucleus is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></math></p><p>Also, let us assume that the initial and the final velocities&nbsp;of the neutron are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;respectively.&nbsp;</p><p>Using the formula of&nbsp;final velocity for a perfectly elastic collision we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"
  }
